  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "ES-C60-bastante",
      "sequence": 2370,
      "title": "bastante — an ending you can already read",
      "headword": "bastante",
      "romanization": "bastante",
      "gloss": "enough, quite — an ending you already decode, on a verb meaning to suffice, giving a word that means exactly \"sufficing\"",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:4b097097667c06bc",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ending -ante, from chapter fifty-two. Estudiante — the one who studies. It turns a verb into the one doing it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Keep that in mind; it is about to hand you a word for free."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart: bastante",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "There is a verb bastar, to be enough. Put your ending on it:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bast- + -ante becomes bastante, \"sufficing\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So bastante does not mean a lot. It means enough — and from there, quite, fairly. It is the amount that suffices, not the amount that impresses."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Estoy bastante cansado. — I'm quite tired."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You now hold a scale, and it is worth saying out loud in order:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 3,
              "utterances": [
                "poco, little.",
                "bastante, enough, quite.",
                "muy, very."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Notice where bastante sits. English speakers reach for it thinking quite a lot, and land higher than they meant. It is the middle of the scale, not the top — the top is muy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And unlike muy, it is not fussy about what follows: bastante café, bastante grande. Only muy insists on leaning on an adjective or an adverb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "poco, bastante, muy, in order",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *poco*, *bastante*, *muy*, in order]"
            },
            {
